    p('''The source ledger and bounded literature audit through 26 October 2026 retain exact acquisition and access limits. Trask’s accepted main text and accessible publisher sections were inspected; Papas [8] was limited to bibliographic records, abstract and publisher preview. No new references were added for the present extension, and the comparison does not establish priority.''')
    p('''AI assistance was used in literature retrieval, mathematical implementation, numerical checking and drafting. Separate automated review passes are disclosed as internal checks, not independent human scientific review. No new animal or human experiment was performed.''')
    h('10 Conclusion')
    p('''In the proposed BEAM geometry, favorable passive transport delivers 71.53% of a uniform 30-minute production increment by its deadline. Preserving dose while thinning improves delivery, but the nominal 0.60 mm design has little margin. Reoptimization distinguishes the small additional area needed after end reflection from the larger requirements in the selected lower-diffusivity and finite-permeability cases. A minimum permitted thickness can remove every target-meeting design from the sampled family: under S24, hypothetical limits of 0.25 and 0.30 mm leave no 80% solution. The map therefore answers both how much area is needed and whether the requirement is attainable under stated constraints. Independent gel, membrane and allowable-layer measurements, followed by prediction of a held-out geometry without refitting, would identify which part of this map applies to an actual device.''')
